 SiO2alpha NCSU       EVAL-MAY11 Holmes, Al-Qasir, Hehr, Hawari     47 1451    5
 REF. 2 (2008)        DIST-                                         47 1451    6
----ENDF/B-VIII.beta  MATERIAL 47                                   47 1451    7
-----THERMAL NEUTRON SCATTERING DATA                                47 1451    8
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                                 47 1451    9
                                                                    47 1451   10
 Temperatures = 293.6 350 400 500 800 K                             47 1451   11
                                                                    47 1451   12
 History                                                            47 1451   13
 -------                                                            47 1451   14
 This library was produced at North Carolina State University in    47 1451   15
 May 2011.  The VASP and PHONON codes were used to produce the      47 1451   16
 DOS for O-16 and natural Si in SiO2.  The alpha-quartz phase       47 1451   17
 is treated for all temperatures in this library.  The beta-        47 1451   18
 quartz phase is treated for 1000 K and 1100 K in a separate        47 1451   19
 library to allow incorporation of phase-specific Bragg edge        47 1451   20
 energy grids.  The LEAPR module was used to produce File 7         47 1451   21
 MT = 2, 4 data for SiO2 as a mixed moderator.  Modifications to    47 1451   22
 the LEAPR source code were made to calculate the                   47 1451   23
 crystallographic structure factors for alpha-quartz for MT = 2     47 1451   24
 data.  Modifications to the normal LEAPR card input were made      47 1451   25
 to correct for issues with LEAPR that apply only to mixed          47 1451   26
 moderators with non-1:1 stoichiometry.  Details of these           47 1451   27
 modifications can be found in Ref. 1, Appendix A.  By              47 1451   28
 convention, compounds have MAT numbers ranging from 1-99.  This    47 1451   29
 range is subdivided by material category.  The current ENDF        47 1451   30
 manual (BNL-90365-2009 Rev. 2) assigns MAT = 47 to O in SiO2       47 1451   31
 under the Oxygen category (MAT = 45-50) since SiO2 clearly does    47 1451   32
 not fall into any other existing category.  However, note that     47 1451   33
 this library uses MAT = 47 for a whole-molecule treatment of       47 1451   34
 alpha-quartz with Si as the primary scatterer.  Following          47 1451   35
 convention for compounds, ZA = MAT + 100 = 147 is used.  When      47 1451   36
 processing with THERMR, the PENDF file used should be for          47 1451   37
 natural Si (or Si-28, if desired).  Also in THERMR and ACER,       47 1451   38
 MT = 247/248 (which are unassigned and not previously used) may    47 1451   39
 be selected for inelastic/elastic scattering reaction              47 1451   40
 types for alpha-quartz until permanent ENDF reaction type          47 1451   41
 numbers are assigned.  If an ACE library is to be produced,        47 1451   42
 use NMIX = 3 on Card 9 in ACER.  See Ref. 1, Appendix A for        47 1451   43
 explanation.                                                       47 1451   44
                                                                    47 1451   45
 Theory                                                             47 1451   46
 ------                                                             47 1451   47
 Both the alpha and beta polymorphic phases of quartz (SiO2) can    47 1451   48
 be viewed on a hexagonal lattice system and have unit cell         47 1451   49
 stoichiometry of Si3O6 (nine atoms).  (Data in this library is     47 1451   50
 associated with the three-atom SiO2 unit).  Alpha-quartz is of     47 1451   51
 the trigonal crystal system with three-fold symmetry while         47 1451   52
 beta-quartz is of the hexagonal crystal system with six-fold       47 1451   53
 symmetry.  The alpha-quartz to beta-quartz phase transformation    47 1451   54
 occurs completely and almost instantaneously at 846 K and is       47 1451   55
 identically reversible.  The transition occurs through a slight    47 1451   56
 realignment of SiO4 tetrahedra which increases the Si-O-Si bond    47 1451   57
 angle from 144 deg. to 153 deg. and reduces density from about     47 1451   58
 2.65 g/cm^3 to 2.53 g/cm^3.                                        47 1451   59
                                                                    47 1451   60
